      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Hydatid disease of the spine is rare and has a poor prognosis, presenting both diagnostic and therapeutic challenges. The diagnosis is based on epidemiological, clinical, biological and radiological arguments. Treatment is primarily surgical. In this observation we report the case of a 45 years old man hospitalized for back pain with heaviness of lower limbs and upper sphincter disorders. Through this case we emphasize the role of the parasitological laboratory in the diagnosis and management of this disease."},
